    "id": "comms-pastor-letter-3",
    "name": "Pastor Letter 3",
    "subject": "Pastor Letter 3",
    "body": "Dear Pastor,\n\n{{name}} will be returning from {{name}} soon. i58 is committed to do all they can, so that each volunteer serving with i58 has a positive mission experience. Often, their hearts are enlarged with compassion as they serve among the hundreds of fathers and mothers with children and babies living in very difficult and crowded conditions. They begin to realize in new ways how blessed they are to have been born in the US.\n\nOne very important aspect of their mission trip is when they come home. Some volunteers come back with a renewed vision of Jesus Christ. Others come back and feel disconnected to the home church.\n\nSome thoughts and tips that could be a help to them during this time:\n\n• Make a personal call or send a message to welcome them home.\n\n• Acknowledge them by name at church and give a public welcome.\n\n• Ask if they might share a brief testimony or presentation with the church, youth group, school, etc. Try to make a slot for them to do so within 3-4 weeks after returning.\n\n• Invite them for a meal or find a time to sit and listen to their experience.\n\n• Questions that could be asked . . .\n\n• What are some of the best things that happened during your time on the field?\n\n• What were the hardest things?\n\n• What is one of the things that you learned about God?\n\n• What is one of the main things that you learned about yourself?\n\n• How has this changed your view of yourself?\n\n• How has this changed your view of God?\n\n• How can you put the same things to practice here at home?\n\n• How can I pray for you?\n\nThis refugee crisis is one of the largest Muslim migrations in recent history. Most refugees are searching for a safe place to live in peace. Years of war and destruction have taken a toll on them. Many are disillusioned in their religion and are on a search for truth and to know God in reality. Truly, this is one of the most amazing opportunities to share the love of God with Muslims. We believe that God is calling the Church to get involved, and to rise up and show forth the glory of God at this time! Here are a few ways that your church can be involved in this open door of ministry to the Muslims.\n\n1. Invite i58 to do a presentation in your church. Contact PR@i58greece.org\n\n2. Funding Would you consider lifting a church offering for i58? Once or twice a year or quarterly?\n\n3. Volunteer. We continue to need volunteers for all locations in Greece and other countries.",
