    "id": "comms-pastor-letter-4",
    "name": "Pastor Letter 4",
    "subject": "Pastor Letter 4",
    "body": "Dear Pastor,\n\nThe staff at i58 says a big thank you for your willingness to be involved in sending your church members to serve with us. We could not do it properly without the support of the pastors and elders of the volunteers. Your input has been greatly appreciated. It is now several weeks since {{name}} has returned from his/her time in {{name}}. We hope that he/she has been able to be a blessing to the church since coming home.\n\nDo you have any feedback for us as to how we could improve or do a better job with our volunteers? Any thoughts that you would like to share with us?\n\n• How has this trip affected your church member?\n\n• Has it been a positive experience overall?\n\n• Have there been any negative things?\n\n• How is their attitude towards others since coming back?\n\n• Are they a blessing to others?\n\n• Are they involved in ministry to others?\n\n• Have there been any major changes in their lives that are noticeable? Negative or Positive?\n\n• Has i58’s attempts to build the relationship between volunteer and pastor been a blessing?\n\nHave you considered getting more involved as a church in this work? Have you considered regular offerings to support the work of i58? Do you have any couples, families or teachers that could go for three months? Are there other youth that you can recommend?\n\nPlease send any of your feedback to info@i58greece.org or call (717) 314-8425.\n\nWe want to see the Glory of God fill the whole earth!\n\nWe want to see the gospel preached to those who have never heard.\n\nWe want to see their lives changed, becoming followers of the Lamb of God.\n\nWe want to see them take the gospel to their own people in Iraq, Syria, Iran, and Afghanistan, as well as other nations of the world. These are places where Christians cannot easily go.\n\nWe want to see youth become established in the Kingdom of God, become pillars in the churches, take the gospel to the ends of the earth and raise up the foundations of many generations.\n\nBlessings,",
