    "body": "Hello i58 volunteers,\n\nThank you for applying to serve with i58. The communities that we work with are vulnerable people groups. As volunteers we want to be aware of how we could be unknowingly contributing to the problems. Here is a course that explains how volunteers can be more aware of situations and what the appropriate responses are. Enjoy!\n\n• You will first need to make an account (it’s free) with Kaya Connect and then you will be able to complete the course. You will need a stable WiFi connection and a computer. It takes about two hours to complete.\n\nSafeguarding Essentials If the above link does not work, please try this link: https://kayaconnect.org/course/view.php?id=1424\n\n• Click on Register for free to set up your account with your own username and password. Return to the Safeguarding Essentials page and click on Join Course.\n\n• You will need to get your certificate of completion. Click on Claim your completion certificate and follow the instructions to download your certificate. (See attached picture for example)\n\n• Volunteers going to Greece: Once you have downloaded the certificate, upload it using this link. Eurorelief needs the certificate as proof you have passed the training in order for you to be able to go into the camp. Volunteers going to Germany or other countries: Once you have downloaded the certificate, email the PDF file to info@i58global.org.\n\nA few tips from other volunteers:\n\n- complete the course in one sitting if possible (it should only take about an hour)\n\n- use a desktop or laptop not a mobile device.\n\n- when you are in the final section, duplicate your tab at the top of your browser-- then if something goes wrong, you have backup.\n\nPlease complete this training and upload your certificate before arriving at training.\n\nthanks,",
